  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Slope of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>.<p>Slope of a line passing&nbsp;through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>17</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>17</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Since, both lines are perpendicular to each other, so product of slopes will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>17</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>17</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
